    "result": "The migration run is finished, but not fully clean: 24 of 29 units are committed, 3 were given up and 2 were skipped by the planner. The final clean build of the last commit (`76baaf1`) passed all 258 tests at C++20, apart from the caveats below. Everything is on branch `codecoremorph/20261103-123434-ab66` (base `99b3c03`), and your working tree and other branches weren't touched. The full report is at `E:\\codecoremorph-home\\bench\\leveldb\\.codecoremorph\\runs\\20261103-123434-ab66\\report.md`.\n\n**Standard bump (U-0001, commit `26aa30a`):** `CMakeLists.txt` now sets C++20. Only one thing broke: `std::memory_order` became a scoped enum, so `std::memory_order::memory_order_relaxed` in `util/env_posix.cc` and `util/env_windows.cc` became `std::memory_order_relaxed`.\n\n**Typedefs to `using`:** the deterministic tools did U-0002 to U-0005 on their own (9 sites).\n\n**Raw pointers to smart pointers:** 252 of 413 detected sites were converted.\n\n| Unit | Area | Attempts | Commit |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| U-0007 | `DBImpl`, `VersionSet`, `Status`, fault-injection test | 1 | `416c758` |\n| U-0008 | Env helpers, corruption/recovery/env tests | 1 | `f7b465c` |\n| U-0009 | table cache, `Table`, `Block`, merging iterator, iterator cleanup list | 3 | `75cfd28` |\n| U-0010 | `IteratorWrapper` | 1 | `c5fd4ce` |\n| U-0011 | `Arena` | 1 | `5dda657` |\n| U-0012 | log reader, repairer, dump tool, log tests | 1 | `25d3671` |\n| U-0013 | C API internals, `db_test`, `bloom_test` | 1 | `8e34ccf` |\n| U-0014 | in-memory Env and its test | 1 | `ccaeacb` |\n| U-0015 | LRU cache hash table, cache tests | 1 | `964e700` |\n| U-0016 | `PosixLogger` | 1 | `1a9b6bb` |\n| U-0018 | `BuildTable`, `ReadBlock`, `TableBuilder`, `table_test` | 2 | `cca6eab` |\n| U-0019 | `LookupKey` | 1 | `0fa44b0` |\n| U-0020 | `MemTable::NewIterator` | 1 | `a4d368f` |\n| U-0023 | `DBIter` | 1 | `2016924` |\n| U-0024 to U-0028 | `version_set_test`, issue tests, `env_posix_test` | 1, 1, 1, 1, 2 | `1eca8c4` \u2026 `76baaf1` |\n\n**Interface changes to review:**\n- **Public headers, private parts only:** `status.h`, `iterator.h`, `table.h` and `table_builder.h` now hold `unique_ptr` members. The API is the same, but code compiled against the old headers isn't binary-compatible.\n- **Internal functions that now return `std::unique_ptr`:** `VersionSet::PickCompaction`, `CompactRange`, `MakeInputIterator` and `MemTable::NewIterator`. All their callers are updated.\n\n**Pointers left raw on purpose:** converting these would change the public API or break an existing ownership scheme:\n- objects handed out through the Env `T**` out-parameters and `DB::Open`'s `DB**`;\n- the public `Iterator*`, `NewLRUCache` and `NewBloomFilterPolicy` factories;\n- the C API handles;\n- the ref-counted `MemTable`, `Version`, `FileMetaData` and memenv `FileState`;\n- the cache's deleter callbacks.\n\n**Units given up (each with its reason in the report):**\n- **U-0017 (`env_posix.cc`):** every site is an object handed across the public Env API.\n- **U-0021 (`snapshot.h`):** an intrusive circular list whose snapshots are handed out through `DB::GetSnapshot`/`ReleaseSnapshot`.\n- **U-0022 (`version_edit`):** all 12 hits were false positives on the name `deleted_files_`; there was nothing to convert.\n\n**Skipped by the planner:** U-0006 and U-0029, because `include/leveldb/c.h` is shared with C. No units were created for concepts, because the detector found no sites.\n\n**What the verification doesn't cover:**\n- **Excused tests:** `env_test` and `EnvTest.ReadWrite` already failed or were flaky before the migration, so they weren't checked.\n- **A pre-existing flaky race:** `EnvTest.ReadWrite` and `EnvPosixTest.TestOpenOnRead` both use `<test dir>/open_on_read.txt`, and ctest runs the two test binaries in parallel. It made attempts fail in U-0009, U-0018 and U-0028, and those passed on re-run without functional changes. Giving the two tests different file names would fix it.\n- **Not compiled by this build:** `util/env_windows.cc` (the `memory_order` fix) is unverified and should be built on Windows. `util/windows_logger.h` still has the raw buffer pattern that U-0016 converted in the POSIX logger.\n\nTo review: `git log 99b3c03..codecoremorph/20261103-123434-ab66` (one commit per unit) or `git diff 99b3c03 codecoremorph/20261103-123434-ab66`. I haven't merged or pushed anything.\n\nIf this needs to go to someone else, I can turn the report into a shareable page."
